        "code": "gsap_repeated_fromto_without_baseline",
        "severity": "warning",
        "message": "3 tl.fromTo() calls target \".pair\" with no stable baseline. The last-authored fromTo \"from\" values become the element's resting state for any seek before the first tween actually runs, because GSAP applies fromTo from-values at authoring time (immediateRender), not at tween position.",
        "selector": ".pair",
        "dataAttributes": {},
        "sourceFile": "/Users/ayumu/orca/projects/meeting-translater/brag-output/composition/index.html",
        "bbox": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0,
          "width": 0,
          "height": 0
        },
        "time": 0,
        "fixHint": "Add `immediateRender: false` to every fromTo except the earliest-positioned one (at 4.39s), so pre-first-tween seeks keep its \"from\" values. A hiding `tl.set(..., 0)` baseline trips gsap_timeline_set_initial_hide, and a `gsap.set` authored before the fromTo calls is overwritten by them."
      },
      {
